{"title": "Sectional Mock #44 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A 255-m long train is running at a speed of 72 km/h. It crosses a platform of length 745 m in:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>255 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; 745 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["53 seconds", "40 seconds", "50 seconds", "51 seconds"], "options_hi": ["53 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "50 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "51 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Length of train = 255 m</p><p>Length of platform = 745 m</p><p>Speed = 72 * 5/18 = 20 m/s</p><p>Time = (255 + 745)/20 = 50 seconds</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Length of train = 255 m</p><p>Length of platform = 745 m</p><p>Speed = 72 * 5/18 = 20 m/s</p><p>Time = (255 + 745)/20 = 50 seconds</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A and pipe B can fill a tank in 18 minutes and 72 minutes respectively. There is an outlet pipe C which can empty the tank in 144 minutes. Find the time taken to fill the tank if all three pipes are opened together.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 18 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2324;&#2352; 72 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 144 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["17 minutes", "13 minutes", "14 minutes", "16 minutes"], "options_hi": ["17 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "13 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "14 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "16 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 18, 72 and 144 = 144 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A = 144/18 = 8 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe B = 144/72 = 2 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe C = 144/144 = 1 unit</p><p>Required time = 144/(8 + 2 - 1) = 144/9 </p><p>=&gt; 16 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Capacity of tank = LCM of 18, 72 and 144 = 144 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A = 144/18 = 8 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe B = 144/72 = 2 unit</p><p>Efficiency of pipe C = 144/144 = 1 unit</p><p>Required time = 144/(8 + 2 - 1) = 144/9 </p><p>=&gt; 16 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>Let there are two numbers A and B such that difference between them is 52 and A = B/3. Find the value of A.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 52 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; A = B/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["13", "26", "39", "24"], "options_hi": ["13", "26", "39", "24"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given B = 3A</p><p>Also given B  -  A = 52</p><p>3A  -  A = 52</p><p>A = 26</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given B = 3A</p><p>Also given B  -  A = 52</p><p>3A  -  A = 52</p><p>A = 26</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 729X<sup>3</sup>  -  125Y<sup>3</sup> = (AX + BY)(CX<sup>2</sup>  -  DY<sup>2</sup> + 45XY) where A, B, C and D are integers, then what is the value of 7A + B  -  C - D?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 729X<sup>3</sup> - 125Y<sup>3</sup> = (AX + BY)(CX<sup>2</sup> - DY<sup>2</sup> + 45XY) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; A, B, C &#2324;&#2352; D &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; 7A + B - C - D &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3", "2", "1", "4"], "options_hi": ["3", "2", "1", "4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>729X<sup>3</sup>  -  125Y<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 729X<sup>3</sup> + (-125Y<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>= (9X)<sup>3</sup> + (-5Y)<sup>3</sup></p><p>= (9X - 5Y)(81X<sup>2</sup> + 25Y<sup>2</sup> + 45XY)</p><p>= (9X + (-5)Y)(81X<sup>2</sup>  -  (-25Y<sup>2</sup>) + 45XY)</p><p>= (AX + BY)(CX<sup>2</sup>  -  DY<sup>2</sup> + 45XY),</p><p>Therefore A = 9, B = -5, C = 81, D = -25</p><p>7A + B  -  C - D = 63  -  5  -  81 + 25 = 58  -  56 = 2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>729X<sup>3</sup>  -  125Y<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 729X<sup>3</sup> + (-125Y<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>= (9X)<sup>3</sup> + (-5Y)<sup>3</sup></p><p>= (9X - 5Y)(81X<sup>2</sup> + 25Y<sup>2</sup> + 45XY)</p><p>= (9X + (-5)Y)(81X<sup>2</sup>  -  (-25Y<sup>2</sup>) + 45XY)</p><p>= (AX + BY)(CX<sup>2</sup>  -  DY<sup>2</sup> + 45XY),</p><p>Therefore A = 9, B = -5, C = 81, D = -25</p><p>7A + B  -  C - D = 63  -  5  -  81 + 25 = 58  -  56 = 2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B started a business by investing &#8377;3000 and &#8377;3600 respectively. After 10 months, B left the business. If the total profit received after one year is &#8377;980, then what is the share of profit received by A?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#8377;3000 &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;3600 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 10 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, B &#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#8377;980 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;520", "&#8377;490", "&#8377;400", "&#8377;550"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;520", "&#8377;490", "&#8377;400", "&#8377;550"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of share of profit of A and B = (3000*12) : (3600*10) = 1:1</p><p>Total profit received after one year = &#8377;980</p><p>Share of profit of B = 980 * 1/2 = &#8377;490</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of share of profit of A and B = (3000*12) : (3600*10) = 1:1</p><p>Total profit received after one year = &#8377;980</p><p>Share of profit of B = 980 * 1/2 = &#8377;490</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of number of students in section A to section B is 9: 11. Section B has 28 more students than section A. Find the total number of students in both sections.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:11 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 28 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["320", "240", "300", "280"], "options_hi": ["320", "240", "300", "280"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let number of students in section A and section B be 9X and 11X respectively.</p><p>Given,</p><p>11X  -  9X = 28</p><p>X = 14</p><p>Total number of students = 9X + 11X = 20X = 20 * 14 = 280</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let number of students in section A and section B be 9X and 11X respectively.</p><p>Given,</p><p>11X  -  9X = 28</p><p>X = 14</p><p>Total number of students = 9X + 11X = 20X = 20 * 14 = 280</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following line graph shows the number of patients admitted in 2023 and the bar graph given below shows the number of patients admitted in 2024 in different hospitals.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 14\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 15\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image015.png\"></p><p>How many hospitals had patient admissions in 2024 that exceeded the average number of admissions in 2023 across all five hospitals?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; 2023 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368; &#2350;&#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; 2024 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2309;&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368; &#2350;&#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 14\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 15\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image015.png\"></p><p>2024 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2352;&#2368;&#2332;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2332;&#2379; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2309;&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 2023 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "3", "1", "2"], "options_hi": ["4", "3", "1", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Average number of patients admitted in all five hospitals in 2023 = (258 + 155 + 450 + 617 + 520)/5 = 400</p><p>The hospitals in which the number of patients admitted in 2024 is above 400 are K, M and N i.e. 3 hospitals</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Average number of patients admitted in all five hospitals in 2023 = (258 + 155 + 450 + 617 + 520)/5 = 400</p><p>The hospitals in which the number of patients admitted in 2024 is above 400 are K, M and N i.e. 3 hospitals</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The difference between compound interest and simple interest on a certain sum of money for 3 years at 10% p.a. is Rs. 1178. Find the principal.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 10% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;.1178 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2343;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.38000", "Rs.36000", "Rs.35000", "Rs.40000"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.38000", "&#2352;&#2369;.36000", "&#2352;&#2369;.35000", "&#2352;&#2369;.40000"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the principal be P.</p><p>S.I. for 3 years = 10% &times; 3P = 0.3P</p><p>C.I. for 3 years = P [(1.1)<sup>3</sup>-1]</p><p>0.331P &ndash; 0.3P = 1178</p><p>P = Rs.38000</p><p>Hence, option a.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the principal be P.</p><p>S.I. for 3 years = 10% &times; 3P = 0.3P</p><p>C.I. for 3 years = P [(1.1)<sup>3</sup>-1]</p><p>0.331P &ndash; 0.3P = 1178</p><p>P = Rs.38000</p><p>Hence, option a.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Evaluate</p><p><table style=\"border:none\">    <tr><td style=\"border-bottom:solid 1px black;text-align:center\"><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><table style=\"border:none\">    <tr><td style=\"border-bottom:solid 1px black;text-align:center\"><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["17/4", "9/2", "13/3", "15/4"], "options_hi": ["17/4", "9/2", "13/3", "15/4"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>\"</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/1517cf1a520ec5ab39c2eb3c41b52223.png\"> </p><p>= 17/4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>\"</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/1517cf1a520ec5ab39c2eb3c41b52223.png\"> </p><p>= 17/4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The diameter and the slant height of a conical tent are 16 m and 5.6 m respectively. What length of cloth having a width of 4 m is needed to make the tent?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2306;&#2348;&#2370; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 16 m &#2324;&#2352; 5.6 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2306;&#2348;&#2370; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 4 m &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2375; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["35.2 m", "32.5 m", "32 m", "35 m"], "options_hi": ["35.2 m", "32.5 m", "32 m", "35 m"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Curved surface area of conical tent = area of cloth</p><p>&#960; * radius of tent * slant height of tent = length of cloth * breadth of cloth</p><p>22/7 * (16/2) * 5.6 = length of cloth * 4</p><p>Length of cloth = 35.2 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Curved surface area of conical tent = area of cloth</p><p>&#960; * radius of tent * slant height of tent = length of cloth * breadth of cloth</p><p>22/7 * (16/2) * 5.6 = length of cloth * 4</p><p>Length of cloth = 35.2 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A can fill a cistern in 4 hours and Pipe B can fill the same cistern in 5 hours. Pipe C can empty a full cistern in 3 hours. If all three pipes are opened together, then the time (in minutes) taken to fill the tank is: (round to the nearest minute)</p>", "q_hi": "&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;: (&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350; &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2340;&#2325;)", "options_en": ["625", "465", "800", "514"], "options_hi": ["625", "465", "800", "514"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Capacity of cistern = LCM of 4, 5 &amp; 3 = 60 units</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A = 60/4 = 15 units/hour</p><p>Efficiency of pipe B = 60/5 = 12 unit/hour</p><p>Efficiency of pipe C = 60/3 = 20 unit/hour</p><p>Required time = 60/(15 + 12  -  20) = 60/7</p><p>=&gt; 60/7 * 60 &#8776; 514 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Capacity of cistern = LCM of 4, 5 &amp; 3 = 60 units</p><p>Efficiency of pipe A = 60/4 = 15 units/hour</p><p>Efficiency of pipe B = 60/5 = 12 unit/hour</p><p>Efficiency of pipe C = 60/3 = 20 unit/hour</p><p>Required time = 60/(15 + 12  -  20) = 60/7</p><p>=&gt; 60/7 * 60 &#8776; 514 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A construction company is working on an unfinished skyscraper. From a point 198 meters away from its base, the angle of elevation to the current top of the skyscraper is 30&deg;. The company plans to increase the height of the building so that, from the same observation point, the new angle of elevation to the top will be 60&deg;. Determine how much additional height must be added to the skyscraper. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2327;&#2327;&#2344;&#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 198 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2327;&#2327;&#2344;&#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 30&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2309;&#2357;&#2354;&#2379;&#2325;&#2344; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 60&deg; &#2361;&#2379;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2327;&#2327;&#2344;&#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2311;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; </p>", "options_en": ["396&radic;3 m", "198&radic;3 m", "594&radic;3 m", "132&radic;3 m"], "options_hi": ["396&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;", "198&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;", "594&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;", "132&radic;3 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the current height and final height of the skyscraper be 'X' m and 'Y' m respectively.</p><p>tan 30&deg; = Perpendicular/ Base</p><p>1/&radic;3 = X/198</p><p>X = 198/&radic;3 m</p><p>tan 60&deg; = Y/198</p><p>&radic;3 = Y/198</p><p>Y = 198&radic;3 m</p><p>Hence, the additional height = 198&radic;3  -  198/&radic;3</p><p>= (594  -  198)/&radic;3</p><p>= 396/&radic;3</p><p>= 132&radic;3 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the current height and final height of the skyscraper be 'X' m and 'Y' m respectively.</p><p>tan 30&deg; = Perpendicular/ Base</p><p>1/&radic;3 = X/198</p><p>X = 198/&radic;3 m</p><p>tan 60&deg; = Y/198</p><p>&radic;3 = Y/198</p><p>Y = 198&radic;3 m</p><p>Hence, the additional height = 198&radic;3  -  198/&radic;3</p><p>= (594  -  198)/&radic;3</p><p>= 396/&radic;3</p><p>= 132&radic;3 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 4x  -  3/4x = 7, then what is the value of 64x<sup>2</sup> + 9/4x<sup>2</sup> = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 4x - 3/4x = 7, &#2340;&#2379; 64x<sup>2</sup> + 9/4x<sup>2</sup> = &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["196", "224", "210", "220"], "options_hi": ["196", "224", "210", "220"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>4x  -  3/4x = 7</p><p>On multiplying 2 both sides:-</p><p>8x  -  3/2x = 14</p><p>Squaring both sides  -  </p><p>64x<sup>2</sup> + 9/4x<sup>2</sup>  -  24 = 196</p><p>64x<sup>2</sup> + 9/4x<sup>2</sup> = 220</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>4x  -  3/4x = 7</p><p>On multiplying 2 both sides:-</p><p>8x  -  3/2x = 14</p><p>Squaring both sides  -  </p><p>64x<sup>2</sup> + 9/4x<sup>2</sup>  -  24 = 196</p><p>64x<sup>2</sup> + 9/4x<sup>2</sup> = 220</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of [(1024)<sup>x/5</sup>  X  (4)<sup>4x-1</sup>]/[64<sup>x</sup>  X  (16)<sup>x-1</sup>]?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>[(1024)<sup>x/5</sup> X (4)<sup>4x-1</sup>]/[64<sup>x</sup> X (16)<sup>x-1</sup>] &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4", "16", "1/4", "1/16"], "options_hi": ["4", "16", "1/4", "1/16"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>(1024)<sup>x/5</sup> = (4<sup>5</sup>)<sup>x/5</sup></p><p>64<sup>x</sup> = 4<sup>3x</sup>, 16<sup>x-1</sup> = (4<sup>2</sup>)<sup>x-1</sup></p><p>Put these values in equation,</p><p>= [(4<sup>5</sup>)<sup>x/5</sup>  X  (4)<sup>4x-1</sup>]/[ 4<sup>3x</sup>  X  (4<sup>2</sup>)<sup>x-1</sup></p><p>= 4<sup>x + 4x  -  1 </sup>/ 4<sup>3x + 2x  -  2</sup></p><p>= 4<sup>5x -1</sup> / 4<sup>5x -2</sup></p><p>= 4<sup>5x -1 -5x +2</sup> = 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(1024)<sup>x/5</sup> = (4<sup>5</sup>)<sup>x/5</sup></p><p>64<sup>x</sup> = 4<sup>3x</sup>, 16<sup>x-1</sup> = (4<sup>2</sup>)<sup>x-1</sup></p><p>Put these values in equation,</p><p>= [(4<sup>5</sup>)<sup>x/5</sup>  X  (4)<sup>4x-1</sup>]/[ 4<sup>3x</sup>  X  (4<sup>2</sup>)<sup>x-1</sup></p><p>= 4<sup>x + 4x  -  1 </sup>/ 4<sup>3x + 2x  -  2</sup></p><p>= 4<sup>5x -1</sup> / 4<sup>5x -2</sup></p><p>= 4<sup>5x -1 -5x +2</sup> = 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>ABC is an equilateral triangle. P, Q, and R are the mid-points of sides AB, BC and CA, respectively. If the length of the side of the triangle ABC is 11 cm, then the area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of &#9651;PQR is:</p>", "q_hi": "ABC &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; AB, BC &#2324;&#2352; CA &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;-&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#9651;PQR &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:", "options_en": ["21&radic;3/16", "11&radic;3/16", "121&radic;3/16", "111&radic;3/16"], "options_hi": ["21&radic;3/16", "11&radic;3/16", "121&radic;3/16", "111&radic;3/16"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Area of triangle PQR = (1/4)  X  Area of triangle ABC</p><p>Area of an equilateral triangle = (&radic;3 / 4)  X  a&#178;, (where 'a' is the side length).</p><p>For triangle ABC, a = 11 cm </p><p>so:</p><p>Area of triangle ABC = (&radic;3 / 4)  X  (11)&#178; = (&radic;3 / 4)  X  121 = (121&radic;3) / 4</p><p>Now, since triangle PQR is formed by joining the midpoints of triangle ABC, its area is 1/4th of the area of triangle ABC:</p><p>Area of triangle PQR = (1/4)  X  (121&radic;3) / 4 = (121&radic;3) / 16</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of triangle PQR = (1/4)  X  Area of triangle ABC</p><p>Area of an equilateral triangle = (&radic;3 / 4)  X  a&#178;, (where 'a' is the side length).</p><p>For triangle ABC, a = 11 cm </p><p>so:</p><p>Area of triangle ABC = (&radic;3 / 4)  X  (11)&#178; = (&radic;3 / 4)  X  121 = (121&radic;3) / 4</p><p>Now, since triangle PQR is formed by joining the midpoints of triangle ABC, its area is 1/4th of the area of triangle ABC:</p><p>Area of triangle PQR = (1/4)  X  (121&radic;3) / 4 = (121&radic;3) / 16</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B can do a job in 20 days and 30 days respectively. They work together for 6 days, then C; who alone takes 60 days to complete the job joins them. How many more days are needed to finish the work?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 20 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; 30 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; 6 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; C, &#2332;&#2379; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 60 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2332;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "5", "6", "7"], "options_hi": ["4", "5", "6", "7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total Work = L.C.M of 20, 30 and 60 = 60 Units</p><p>Efficiency of A = 60/20 = 3 Units/day</p><p>Efficiency of B = 60/30 = 2 Units/day</p><p>Efficiency of C = 60/60 = 1 Units/day</p><p>Total Work done A and B in 6days = (3 + 2)* 6 = 30 Units</p><p>Remaining = 30 units</p><p>With C, days needed= 30/(3+2+1) = 30/6 = 5 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total Work = L.C.M of 20, 30 and 60 = 60 Units</p><p>Efficiency of A = 60/20 = 3 Units/day</p><p>Efficiency of B = 60/30 = 2 Units/day</p><p>Efficiency of C = 60/60 = 1 Units/day</p><p>Total Work done A and B in 6days = (3 + 2)* 6 = 30 Units</p><p>Remaining = 30 units</p><p>With C, days needed= 30/(3+2+1) = 30/6 = 5 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of &#952; from the given expression:</p><p><div>&nbsp;cosec<sup>2</sup> &theta; -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#952; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;-</p><p><div>&nbsp;cosec<sup>2</sup> &theta; -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2", "options_en": ["30&deg;", "45&deg;", "75&deg;", "15&deg;"], "options_hi": ["30<sup>0</sup>", "45<sup>0</sup>", "75<sup>0</sup>", "15<sup>0</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>cosec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  2/sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1</p><p>=> 2/sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; = cosec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  1</p><p>=> 2/sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; = cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;</p><p>=> 2 = sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; * cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;</p><p>=> sin<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1/2</p><p>=> sin&#952; = 1/&radic;2</p><p>=> &#952; = 45&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>cosec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  2/sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1</p><p>=> 2/sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; = cosec<sup>2</sup>&#952;  -  1</p><p>=> 2/sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; = cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;</p><p>=> 2 = sec<sup>2</sup>&#952; * cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;</p><p>=> sin<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1/2</p><p>=> sin&#952; = 1/&radic;2</p><p>=> &#952; = 45&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two numbers are in the ratio of 5 : 13. LCM of the numbers is 520. Find the smaller number among them.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 5 : 13 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; LCM 520 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["52", "40", "42", "48"], "options_hi": ["52", "40", "42", "48"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let, the numbers be 5x and 13x.</p><p>LCM = 65x</p><p>65x = 520</p><p>=> x = 8</p><p>Smaller number = 5 * 8 = 40</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, the numbers be 5x and 13x.</p><p>LCM = 65x</p><p>65x = 520</p><p>=> x = 8</p><p>Smaller number = 5 * 8 = 40</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train 800 meters long crosses a platform whose length is 1400 meters in 20 seconds. If a man is running at a speed of 8 m/s towards the train and the front of the train is 177 meters away from the man, then in how much time will the train and the man meet each other?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>800 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1400 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335;&#2347;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 8 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 177 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["1.2 seconds", "1.5 seconds", "1.1 seconds", "1.0 seconds"], "options_hi": ["1.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "1.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "1.1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "1.0 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The train can cover (800 + 1400) m distance in 20 seconds which means the speed of the train = 2200/20 = 110 m/s</p><p>Relative speed of the man and train = 110 + 8 = 118 m/s</p><p>To cover the distance of 177 meters, it will take = 177/118 = 1.5 seconds</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The train can cover (800 + 1400) m distance in 20 seconds which means the speed of the train = 2200/20 = 110 m/s</p><p>Relative speed of the man and train = 110 + 8 = 118 m/s</p><p>To cover the distance of 177 meters, it will take = 177/118 = 1.5 seconds</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the average of 5 numbers 2m  -  1, 56, 128, 11 and 3m is 47.8, then the value of 'm' is equal to  - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 5 &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; 2m - 1, 56, 128, 11 &#2324;&#2352; 3m &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 47.8 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'm' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["11", "9", "8", "10"], "options_hi": ["11", "9", "8", "10"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Average = (sum of observations)/(number of observations)</p><p>Then, 47.8 = (2m  -  1 + 56 + 128 + 11 + 3m)/5</p><p>239 = 5m + 194</p><p>5m = 45</p><p><b>m = 9</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Average = (sum of observations)/(number of observations)</p><p>Then, 47.8 = (2m  -  1 + 56 + 128 + 11 + 3m)/5</p><p>239 = 5m + 194</p><p>5m = 45</p><p><b>m = 9</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>After dividing a number successively by 5, 6, and 9, the remainder are 1, 3, and 4. What will be the remainder, if 21 divides the same number (if the last quotient is 3)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; 5, 6 &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; 1, 3 &#2324;&#2352; 4 &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; 21 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; (&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; 3 &#2361;&#2376;) &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "4", "3", "1"], "options_hi": ["2", "4", "3", "1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The last quotient is 3.</p><p>The number that is divided by 9 = 9 x 3 + 4 = 31</p><p>The number that is divided by 6 = 31 x 6 + 3 = 189</p><p>The number that is divided by 5 = 189 x 5 + 3 = 948</p><p>When we divide 948 by 21, we get 3 as a remainder.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The last quotient is 3.</p><p>The number that is divided by 9 = 9 x 3 + 4 = 31</p><p>The number that is divided by 6 = 31 x 6 + 3 = 189</p><p>The number that is divided by 5 = 189 x 5 + 3 = 948</p><p>When we divide 948 by 21, we get 3 as a remainder.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>How much quantity (in kg) of corn flour costing Rs. 63 per kg must be mixed with 40 kg of rice flour of costing Rs. 36 per kg, so that on selling the mixture at Rs. 58.5 per kg, there is a gain of 30%?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>63 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2325;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; 36 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; 40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 58.5 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["20 kg", "40 kg", "60 kg", "50 kg"], "options_hi": ["20 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;", "40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;", "60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;", "50 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let k kg of corn flour is added. </p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(k * 63 + 40 * 36)/(k + 40) = 58.5 * 100/130</p><p>=&gt; (63k + 1440)/(k + 40) = 45</p><p>=&gt; 63k + 1440 = 45k + 1800</p><p>=&gt; 18k = 360</p><p>=&gt; k = 20 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let k kg of corn flour is added. </p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(k * 63 + 40 * 36)/(k + 40) = 58.5 * 100/130</p><p>=&gt; (63k + 1440)/(k + 40) = 45</p><p>=&gt; 63k + 1440 = 45k + 1800</p><p>=&gt; 18k = 360</p><p>=&gt; k = 20 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Water from 'N' small cylindrical mugs each of radius and height 15 cm and 14 cm respectively is poured into a large cuboidal pool of dimension 2 m * 4.5 m * 2.2 m to completely fill it, find the value of N.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>'N' &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 15 cm &#2324;&#2352; 14 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2352; 2 m * 4.5 m * 2.2 m &#2310;&#2351;&#2366;&#2350; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2346;&#2370;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["24 * 10<sup>2</sup>", "3 * 10<sup>3</sup>", "2 * 10<sup>3</sup>", "1440"], "options_hi": ["24 * 10<sup>2</sup>", "3 * 10<sup>3</sup>", "2 * 10<sup>3</sup>", "1440"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of one small mug = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = (22/7) * 15<sup>2</sup> * 14 = 225 * 44 = (900/4) * 44 = 9900 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Volume of pool = (2 * 100) * (4.5 * 100) * (2.2 * 100) = 19.8 * 10<sup>6</sup> cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Volume of N small mugs = Volume of pool</p><p>N * 9900 = 19.8 * 10<sup>6</sup></p><p>N * 9900 = 19800 * 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>N = 2 * 10<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of one small mug = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h = (22/7) * 15<sup>2</sup> * 14 = 225 * 44 = (900/4) * 44 = 9900 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Volume of pool = (2 * 100) * (4.5 * 100) * (2.2 * 100) = 19.8 * 10<sup>6</sup> cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Volume of N small mugs = Volume of pool</p><p>N * 9900 = 19.8 * 10<sup>6</sup></p><p>N * 9900 = 19800 * 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>N = 2 * 10<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x<sup>16</sup>  -  617x<sup>8</sup> + 16 = 0, and x &gt; 0, then find the value of x<sup>2</sup> +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x<sup>16</sup> - 617x<sup>8</sup> + 16 = 0 &#2324;&#2352; x &gt; 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x<sup>2</sup> + <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2", "options_en": ["&radic;31", "&radic;29", "&radic;33", "&radic;26"], "options_hi": ["&radic;31", "&radic;29", "&radic;33", "&radic;26"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given,</p><p><img width=139 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=115 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=97 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=120 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=119 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=89 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=109 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=99 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image009.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given,</p><p><img width=139 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=115 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=97 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=120 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=119 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=89 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=109 height=45 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=99 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16030/image009.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Evaluate for ?: [(&radic;4096 &div; 8) + (2<sup>4</sup> &div; 2)]  X  &#8731;? = 48</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;: [(&radic;4096 &div; 8) + (2<sup>4</sup> &div; 2)] X &#8731;? = 48</p>", "options_en": ["27", "8", "18", "15"], "options_hi": ["27", "8", "18", "15"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>&radic;4096 = 64; 64 &div; 8 = 8</p><p>2<sup>4</sup> = 16; 16 &div; 2 = 8</p><p>8 + 8 = 16</p><p>16  X  &#8731;? = 48 =&gt; &#8731;? = 3 =&gt; ? = 27</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&radic;4096 = 64; 64 &div; 8 = 8</p><p>2<sup>4</sup> = 16; 16 &div; 2 = 8</p><p>8 + 8 = 16</p><p>16  X  &#8731;? = 48 =&gt; &#8731;? = 3 =&gt; ? = 27</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}]}